WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.245
In 2022, 1.12 billion people lived
in slums or informal settlements:

2
00:00:06.295 --> 00:00:11.050
24.8 per cent of the
world's urban population.

3
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.350
Now zoom into one city:
Mumbai, Census 2011.

4
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.830
In D ward, 1 in 10 people lived in slums.

5
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:22.110
In M East ward, more than 3 in 4 did.

6
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.470
Same city, same census.

7
00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.270
So why such a gap?

8
00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.410
Do rich wards ban slums?

9
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.950
In this mission, you'll separate poverty,

10
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.670
deprivation and informality, from Mumbai's
wards to England's Index of Multiple

11
00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:37.070
Deprivation.

12
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.670
Then you'll trace the
cycle of deprivation,

13
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:43.490
map crime, and judge how
Glasgow tackled violence.

14
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:48.430
Your mission: explain why the slum share
was so much higher in M East ward than

15
00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.400
in D ward.
